  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "If \\(a\\ne b,\\) \\(a^3-b^3=19x^3,\\) and \\(a-b=x,\\) which of the following conclusions is correct?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(a=3x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(a=3x\\) or \\(a=-2x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(a=-3x\\) or \\(a=2x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(a=3x\\) or \\(a=2x\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(a=2x\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring and dividing by \\(x\\ne0\\) gives \\(a^2+ab+b^2=19x^2.\\) With \\(b=a-x,\\) \\[ 3a^2-3ax+x^2=19x^2, \\] so \\[ \\begin{aligned} a^2-ax-6x^2&=0,\\\\ (a-3x)(a+2x)&=0. \\end{aligned} \\] Hence \\(a=3x\\) or \\(a=-2x.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor \\(a^3-b^3\\) and use \\(x=a-b\\ne0\\)",
        "Substitute \\(b=a-x\\) after dividing by \\(x\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
